d heroine.\n\n### **YA Fantasy (Great for All Ages):**\n13. **\"Harry Potter and the Sorcerer\u2019s Stone\"** by J.K. Rowling \u2013 A must-read for any fantasy fan.\n14. **\"Six of Crows\"** by Leigh Bardugo \u2013 A heist story with a found-family crew in a rich, magical world.\n15. **\"The Cruel Prince\"** by Holly Black \u2013 A dark faerie tale full of political intrigue and morally ambiguous characters.\n\n### **Standalone Fantasy (If You Prefer a Single Book):**\n16. **\"The Night Circus\"** by Erin Morgenstern \u2013 A magical, dreamlike competition between two illusionists.\n17. **\"Uprooted\"** by Naomi Novik \u2013 A dark fairy-tale-like story with a strong heroine and a mysterious mentor.\n18. **\"The Last Unicorn\"** by Peter S. Beagle \u2013 A poetic, timeless fantasy about a unicorn\u2019s journey to discover her kind.\n\n### **Newer/Under-the-Radar Gems:**\n19. **\"The Justice of Kings\"** by Richard Swan \u2013 A fresh take on dark fantasy with a judicial system where traveling magistrates act as judge, jury, and executioner.\n20. **\"Legends & Lattes\"** by Travis Baldree \u2013 A cozy, heartwarming fantasy about an orc opening a coffee shop.\n\nWould you like something more specific (e.g., romance-heavy, low-magic, non-Western-inspired, etc.)? Or do any of these catch your interest?"}}
